      "title": "Use one logarithmic variable",
      "body": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></math>, so its square is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "The equation becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.",
      "pitfall": "The minus sign inside a squared logarithm disappears.",
      "pause": "Which substitution turns this into a quadratic?",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l06",
          "reminder": "Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> while preserving the positive argument restriction."
        }
